	<!--
	    Required, not optional. The standalone is an EFFECT, so JUCE opens an
	    audio INPUT device on launch. Under the hardened runtime macOS
	    terminates a process that requests input access without a usage
	    description - the app would not merely fail to record, it would die on
	    first launch on a customer's machine. The plug-in formats do not need
	    this: they inherit the host's permission.
	-->
	<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
	<string>SourceGlo Pro needs access to your audio input so the standalone application can process live audio from your interface.</string>
</dict>
